Alembic migrations (async, asyncpg). The schema is managed ONLY by migrations;
the application does not create tables at startup.

DATABASE_URL is read from application settings (environment / .env), not from
alembic.ini. Run all commands from the backend/ directory:

    alembic upgrade head                              # apply migrations
    alembic downgrade -1                              # roll back one revision
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
    alembic check                                     # fail if models and DB differ

Always review autogenerated migrations by hand (e.g. PostgreSQL ENUM types are
not dropped automatically on downgrade).
